course: dictionary
lesson: 15394
title: Spillage: liquid that has spilled
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A spillage is an amount of liquid, or other stuff, that has spilled out by accident. Spillage can also mean the act of spilling. Look for clues around the word: «The cleaner mopped up the water spillage before anyone slipped.» Mopping up tells you the water had spilled onto the floor.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «The science teacher reported a small chemical spillage at once.» Put in "a small amount of stuff that spilled by accident" and the sentence still makes sense. Chemicals can be dangerous, so the teacher tells someone quickly.
explain: Spillage often appears in phrases such as «oil spillage», «chemical spillage» and «clean up a spillage». Spillage is a noun, so it names a thing or an action.
fact: Spillage is a noun. It names an amount of liquid or stuff that has spilled, or the act of spilling.
fact: «Spillage» means an amount of liquid or other stuff that has spilled out by accident.
fact: In science labs and at school dinners, a spillage must be wiped up quickly to stop slips.
fact: A «spillage kit» holds the things you need to clean up a spill safely.
fact: «Oil spillage» means oil that has escaped into the sea or onto land, and it can harm sea birds and beaches.
exercise: «The cleaner mopped up the water spillage before anyone slipped.» What does spillage mean here? | A type of cleaning cloth | *Liquid that has spilled by accident | A bucket for water | A dry, slippery floor
exercise: «Oil spillage from the ship harmed sea birds on the beach.» What harmed the sea birds? | A ship's bell | A big wave | The sand | *Oil that had spilled out
exercise: «Please use the spillage kit to clean up the juice.» What is a spillage kit for? | Cooking dinner | *Cleaning up a spill | Playing games | Making juice
test: «Warning sign: spillage on the floor.» Why would a sign say this? | *To warn people the floor may be slippery | To advertise a new mop | To tell people the floor is clean | To show where the toilets are
test: «The teacher reported a chemical spillage in the lab at once.» What does reported show? | The teacher made the chemical | The teacher forgot about it | *The teacher told someone about it quickly | The teacher drank the chemical
exam: Which phrase means oil that has spilled into the sea? | school dinner | spillage kit | clean desk | *oil spillage
